# flow_block_begin

- Label: Flow Block Begin
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 5
- Parameters: 6 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/flow_block_begin.html
- Summary (EN): This node marks the start of a Flow simulation block in Copernicus. Flow runs simple 2D simulations of incompressible flowing liquid.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Flow Block Begin ouvre un bloc de simulation de fluide incompressible dans Copernicus, en fournissant les données initiales.

- Inputs meaning: ["color: RGBA layer of initial fluid colors; read on the first frame only", "v: UV layer of initial flow directions; read on the first frame only", "temperature (optional): Mono layer of initial fluid temperatures; read on the first frame only", "feedback: cable fed back to the next iteration; its structure must exactly match the Flow Block End input; read on the first frame only", "passthrough (optional): cable of layers computed outside the simulation and read every frame, useful for animated sources"]

- Key parameters: ["Block Path: path to the matching Flow Block End node, which must be at the same network level", "Buoyancy: strength of the internal buoyancy force; the temperature field is scaled by this value and added to the velocity", "Buoyancy Direction: direction in which higher temperatures move", "Correct Initial Velocity: pressure-projects incoming velocities so they represent valid fluid motion", "Layers to Advect: wire names of the layers advected by the velocity layer; the v layer is always advected"]

- Caveats: ["Flow requires DOP-level permissions; it is not available in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "Time Shift cannot be used inside Copernicus blocks when it needs block inputs at different times; the page suggests Time Pack before Block Begin, wired in as a cable", "Passthrough inputs cannot depend on the simulation results", "Operations that do not depend on previous frames should go before the block so they cook only once"]

